      "The gas savings this produces are the entire reason portable concentrators and small conserving-device-equipped tanks can support a mobile lifestyle at all. A continuous-flow tank sized for a full day of use would be too heavy to carry; the same clinical oxygen delivery through pulse-dose conserving technology can come from a cylinder a fraction of the size, or from a portable concentrator's compressor working within realistic power and weight budgets.",
